  "question": {
    "text": "If $E$ and $F$ are two independent events with $P(E)=0.3$ and $P(E \\cup F)=0.5$, then $P(E / F)-P(F / E)$ equals",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gKUWD",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{7}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LK04y",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{35}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ga4ld",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{70}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "rxcpF",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{7}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text {  } P(E \\cup F)=P(E)+P(F)-P(E \\cap F) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 0.5=0.3+P(F)-P(E) \\cdot P(F) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 0.2=P(F)-0.3 P(F) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow P(F)=\\frac{2}{7}\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nSo, $P(E / F)-P(F / E)=P(E)-P(F)=\\frac{3}{10}-\\frac{2}{7}=\\frac{21-20}{70}=\\frac{1}{70}$",
    "image": null
  },
